{"name":"Create","hex":"#c9cabf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"create","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bring into existence;","To bring into existence out of nothing, without the prior existence of the materials or elements used."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Created, resulting from creation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/create"}],"entries":[{"title":"Creativity","blocks":[{"text":"Creativity is the ability to generate novel and valuable ideas or works through the exercise of imagination. The products of creativity may be classified as either intangible or physical. Intangible products of creativity include ideas, scientific theories, literary works, musical compositions, and jokes. Physical products of creativity include inventions, dishes or meals, pieces of jewelry, costumes, and paintings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Crystal_Clear_app_ktip.svg/330px-Crystal_Clear_app_ktip.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creativity"},{"title":"Characterization","blocks":[{"text":"Characterization or characterisation is the representation of characters in narrative and dramatic works. The term character development is sometimes used as a synonym. This representation may include direct methods like the attribution of qualities in description or commentary, and indirect methods inviting readers to infer qualities from characters' actions, dialogue, or appearance. Such a personage is called a character. Character(s) is an essential narrative element."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Characterization"},{"title":"Create (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Create\"  is a song by Japanese singer-songwriter and musician Gen Hoshino from his fifth studio album, Gen (2025). The theme song to the 35th anniversary of the Nintendo video game Super Mario Bros. (1985), the song first appeared in a June 2020 commercial. Speedstar Records released it as a digital single on February 17, 2021, before a physical double A-sided CD with \"Fushigi\" was issued on June 23, 2021. Inspired by Nintendo's creative philosophy, Hoshino wrote and produced the track, and co-arranged it with Mabanua. A J-pop, progressive pop, and soul song, the lyrics sees Hoshino encouraging listeners to create. It features several references to Nintendo, such as the start-up jingle to their GameCube console, sound effects from Super Mario Bros., and homages to the company's history."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1d/Create_-_Gen_Hoshino_%28cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Create_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4a/Plato-raphael.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4a/Plato-raphael.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Greek philosophers like Plato rejected the concept of creativity, preferring to see art as a form of discovery. When asked in The Republic, \"Will we say, of a painter, that he makes something?\", Plato answers, \"Certainly not, he merely imitates.\"[15]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlato-raphael.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Distributed_network_of_voxel_clusters_associated_with_divergent_thinking.jpg/500px-Distributed_network_of_voxel_clusters_associated_with_divergent_thinking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Distributed_network_of_voxel_clusters_associated_with_divergent_thinking.jpg/500px-Distributed_network_of_voxel_clusters_associated_with_divergent_thinking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Distributed functional brain network associated with divergent thinking","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistributed_network_of_voxel_clusters_associated_with_divergent_thinking.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Training_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg/500px-Training_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Training_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg/1280px-Training_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Training_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg/500px-Training_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Training meeting in an eco-design stainless steel company in Brazil. The leaders, among other things, wish to cheer and encourage the workers in order to achieve a higher level of creativity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraining_meeting_in_an_ecodesign_stainless_steel_company_in_brazil.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Nintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg/500px-Nintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Nintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg/1280px-Nintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Nintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg/500px-Nintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Create\" was inspired by the creative philosophy of Nintendo (headquarters pictured, 2014).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANintendo_Kyoto_Development_Complex_View.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/GameCube-Set.jpg/500px-GameCube-Set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/GameCube-Set.jpg/1280px-GameCube-Set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/GameCube-Set.jpg/500px-GameCube-Set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One critic highlighted the song's vibraphone arrangement of the GameCube start-up jingle (console pictured).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGameCube-Set.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Koji_kondo.jpg/250px-Koji_kondo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/de/Koji_kondo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Koji_kondo.jpg/250px-Koji_kondo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Koji Kondo (pictured 2006), the original composer of Super Mario Bros., played the series' theme during a performance of \"Create\" at the 76th NHK Kōhaku Uta Gassen on New Year's Eve 2025.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoji_kondo.jpg"}],"sounds":{"create":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/En-us-create.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg",